    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1026">

                <pb facs="1067" n="781" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg781"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/2969</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-10-23T18:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 23, 1916, 6 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 6.30 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5070. Your 3968, October 22, 5 p. m. The British Government have made no request
                    of me, but both Government and public are anxious to know precisely what
                    happened and there is no authoritative way to obtain information except by our
                    Government’s making facts known. In cases mentioned by you there would be no
                    objection if no loss of ships nor were lives put in jeopardy [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">sic</hi>]. Since British ships were sunk and British
                    subjects put into small boats, there is a natural curiosity to know precisely
                    what happened and consequent criticism of our Government for not making facts
                    known which can be made known in no other way.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Page</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
